{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Is it not so, if you do well, you shall be lifted up?</b> According to the opinion of the commentators (Onkelos, Rashi, and Radak), שְׂאֵת means 'the lifting up of your sin' (i.e., forgiveness). According to the opinion of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 4:7), שְׂאֵת means 'the lifting up of your face,' corresponding to 'why has your face fallen,' for one who is ashamed casts his face downward, and likewise 'and the light of my face they did not cast down' (Job 29:24), and one who is honored is as though his face is lifted upward; and this is the sense of 'perhaps he will lift my face' (Genesis 32:21), 'you shall not lift the face of the poor' (Leviticus 19:15). And in my opinion, 'if you do well' — you shall have superiority of elevation over your brother, for you are the firstborn, and this is the sense of 'why are you angry,' for it was from shame before his brother that his face fell, and out of jealousy toward him he killed him. And so He said to him: Why are you angry at your brother, and why has your face fallen because of him? Is it not so that if you do well, you shall have superiority of elevation over your brother, and if you do not do well, evil shall not come upon you only in his presence — rather, at the doorway of your house your sin crouches to cause you to stumble in all your ways." "<b>And its desire is toward you</b> — that it will long to cleave to you all the days, but you shall rule over it if you so desire, for you shall improve your ways and remove it from upon you. He taught him about repentance, that it is given into his hand to return at whatever time he wishes, and He will forgive him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The final clause translates the reading according to Ramban's interpretation; the Hebrew reads לא עמו בלבד תבואך רעה, which I render hyper-literally as 'evil shall not come upon you only in his presence,' i.e., not only when you are with him."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:31.921737802Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}